═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

📌 BIAS: Incorrect assumptions in the model
───────────────────────────────────────────
• High Bias = Model makes strong wrong assumptions
• Example: Assuming all birds are small (bias against big birds)
          Model fails to recognize ostriches & penguins

📌 VARIANCE: Model sensitivity to data changes
──────────────────────────────────────────────
• High Variance = Model changes dramatically with small data changes
• Model captures noise and random fluctuations
• Overfits to training data

