5️⃣  REGULARIZATION: Preventing Overfitting
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

What is Regularization?
  → Add penalty to model for being too complex
  → Forces model to learn simpler, more general patterns
  → Improves generalization

3 Main Types:

1️⃣  L1 REGULARIZATION (Lasso) : shift slopes towards x axis 
    • Penalizes sum of absolute weights
    • Can reduce some feature weights to ZERO
    • Useful for feature selection

2️⃣  L2 REGULARIZATION (Ridge) : this also shift slopes towards x axis
    • Penalizes sum of squared weights
    • Spreads weights evenly across features
    • Shrinks weights but rarely to zero

3️⃣  ELASTIC NET
    • Combination of L1 and L2
    • Best of both worlds

REGULARIZATION STRENGTH (λ):
  • λ = 0: No regularization (can overfit)
  • λ = small: Weak regularization
  • λ = medium: Balanced (BEST)
  • λ = large: Strong regularization (can underfit)

