What is Feature Engineering?
  → Process of transforming raw data into meaningful features
  → Makes the model smarter by giving it better inputs

Key Techniques:

📐 ENCODING CATEGORICAL VARIABLES
   └─ Convert text/categories to numbers
   
   a) ONE-HOT ENCODING:
      Example: Color = [Red, Green, Blue]
      Convert to: Color_Red=[1,0,0], Color_Green=[0,1,0], Color_Blue=[0,0,1]
   
   b) LABEL ENCODING:
      Red=0, Green=1, Blue=2 (use for ordinal data)

🔢 SCALING NUMERIC FEATURES
   └─ Make features comparable (same range)
   
   a) NORMALIZATION (0-1 range):
      Formula: (x - min) / (max - min)
      Use when: Data has outliers
   
   b) STANDARDIZATION (mean=0, std=1):
      Formula: (x - mean) / standard_deviation
      Use when: Data is normally distributed

🔗 INTERACTION FEATURES
   └─ Combine features to capture relationships
   
   Example: Create "age × smoker" to capture how smoking affects age groups
   OR: "bmi × smoker" to show interaction effect

🎯 FEATURE SELECTION
   └─ Choose most important features
   
   Benefits:
   ✓ Reduces overfitting
   ✓ Improves model speed
   ✓ Makes model interpretable
   ✓ Removes noise

