What is Cross-Validation?
  → Technique to better evaluate model performance
  → Splits data into multiple folds instead of just train/test
  → Reduces randomness in evaluation

Why Use It?
  ✓ More robust performance estimate
  ✓ Uses data efficiently
  ✓ Detects overfitting better
  ✓ Works well with small datasets

Types of Cross-Validation:

1️⃣  K-FOLD CROSS-VALIDATION (Most Common)
    • Divide data into K equal parts
    • Train on K-1 folds, test on 1 fold
    • Repeat K times, average the results
    Example: 5-fold CV splits data into 5 parts
      Fold 1: Test on part 1, Train on 2,3,4,5
      Fold 2: Test on part 2, Train on 1,3,4,5
      Fold 3: Test on part 3, Train on 1,2,4,5
      Fold 4: Test on part 4, Train on 1,2,3,5
      Fold 5: Test on part 5, Train on 1,2,3,4
      Final Score = Average of all 5 fold scores

2️⃣  STRATIFIED K-FOLD
    • Same as K-fold but maintains class distribution
    • Useful for imbalanced datasets
    • Ensures each fold has similar class proportions

3️⃣  LEAVE-ONE-OUT CV
    • K = number of samples (K-fold where K = n)
    • Computationally expensive but very thorough

