What are Hyperparameters?
  → Settings we configure BEFORE training model
  → NOT learned from data
  → Greatly affect model performance

Examples:
  • Learning rate (how fast model learns)
  • Number of layers (in neural networks)
  • Regularization strength (λ)
  • Number of trees (Random Forest)
  • K value (in K-Means clustering)
  • Max depth (tree depth limit)

Tuning Methods:

1️⃣  GRID SEARCH
    • Try all combinations of hyperparameters
    • Exhaustive but computationally expensive
    Example: Test learning rates [0.001, 0.01, 0.1]
             AND regularization [0.1, 0.5, 1.0]
             → 3 × 3 = 9 combinations to test

2️⃣  RANDOM SEARCH
    • Randomly sample hyperparameter combinations
    • Faster than grid search
    • Often finds good parameters with less computation

3️⃣  BAYESIAN OPTIMIZATION
    • Uses probability to guide search
    • Smarter than random search
    • Most efficient method


