📈 EVALUATION METRICS FOR LINEAR REGRESSION

1. MEAN SQUARED ERROR (MSE)
   • Average of squared differences between actual and predicted
   • Formula: (1/n) * Σ(y_actual - y_pred)²
   • Lower is better
   • Units: Same as target² (e.g., price² if predicting price)

2. ROOT MEAN SQUARED ERROR (RMSE)
   • Square root of MSE
   • Formula: √MSE
   • Better interpretation: Same units as target
   • Lower is better

3. MEAN ABSOLUTE ERROR (MAE)
   • Average absolute difference between actual and predicted
   • Formula: (1/n) * Σ|y_actual - y_pred|
   • Less sensitive to outliers than MSE
   • Lower is better

4. R² SCORE (Coefficient of Determination)
   • What: How much variance in target is explained by model?
   • Range: 0 to 1 (higher is better, negative = worse than average)
   • Formula: 1 - (SS_res / SS_tot)
   • Interpretation:
     * R² = 1.0 → Perfect fit
     * R² = 0.9 → Explains 90% of variance
     * R² = 0.5 → Explains 50% of variance
     * R² = 0.0 → Same as predicting mean
     * R² < 0.0 → Worse than predicting mean

5. ADJUSTED R²
   • Penalizes adding unnecessary features
   • Better for comparing models with different number of features
   • Formula: 1 - [(1 - R²) * (n-1) / (n-p-1)]
   • Where n = samples, p = features

