🎯 EVALUATION METRICS FOR LOGISTIC REGRESSION

1. ACCURACY
   • What: Percentage of correct predictions
   • Formula: (TP + TN) / (TP + TN + FP + FN)
   • Problem: Misleading with imbalanced data
   • Use: When classes are balanced

2. PRECISION
   • What: Of predicted positives, how many are actually positive?
   • Formula: TP / (TP + FP)
   • Use: When False Positives are costly (e.g., spam detection)

3. RECALL (Sensitivity)
   • What: Of actual positives, how many did we find?
   • Formula: TP / (TP + FN)
   • Use: When False Negatives are costly (e.g., disease detection)

4. F1-SCORE
   • What: Harmonic mean of precision and recall
   • Formula: 2 * (Precision * Recall) / (Precision + Recall)
   • Use: When you need balance between precision and recall

5. ROC-AUC
   • What: Area under the ROC curve (Receiver Operating Characteristic)
   • Range: 0 to 1 (higher is better, 0.5 = random)
   • Use: Best metric for binary classification problems

