1️⃣4️⃣  ENSEMBLE METHODS: Combining Multiple Models
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

What is Ensemble Learning?
  → Combine multiple models to get better predictions
  → "Wisdom of crowds" approach
  → Usually outperforms single model

Why Ensemble Works?
  ✓ Different models catch different patterns
  ✓ Reduces variance and bias
  ✓ More robust to outliers
  ✓ Better generalization

Popular Ensemble Methods:

1️⃣  BAGGING (Bootstrap Aggregating)
    • Create multiple subsets of training data (with replacement)
    • Train model on each subset independently
    • Average predictions from all models
    Example: Random Forest uses bagging
    
2️⃣  BOOSTING
    • Train models sequentially
    • Each model focuses on mistakes of previous models
    • Weight observations based on errors
    Examples: AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting, XGBoost
    • Reduces both bias and variance
    
3️⃣  VOTING / AVERAGING
    • Train different model types
    • Average their predictions
    • Works for regression and classification
    Example: Vote with Logistic Regression + Decision Tree + SVM
    
4️⃣  STACKING
    • Train multiple models (base learners)
    • Use their predictions as features for final model (meta-learner)
    • Meta-learner learns optimal way to combine weak learners
    • More sophisticated than voting

