1️⃣7️⃣  LEARNING CURVES: Diagnosing Problems
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

What are Learning Curves?
  → Plot of training error vs validation error vs amount of training data
  → Shows if model has high bias or variance problem

Reading Learning Curves:

UNDERFITTING (High Bias):
  • Both curves HIGH and run parallel
  • No gap between training and validation
  • Solution: Increase model complexity

OVERFITTING (High Variance):
  • Large gap between training and validation curves
  • Training error LOW, validation error HIGH
  • Solution: Reduce complexity or add more data

GOOD FIT:
  • Both curves LOW
  • Small gap between them
  • Both approach similar value

NEED MORE DATA:
  • Curves haven't converged
  • Still room for improvement
  • Add more training data to fix

