1️⃣8️⃣  FEATURE SCALING: WHY & WHEN
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

When Features are NOT Scaled:
  ✗ Features with larger ranges dominate distance calculations
  ✗ Model may perform poorly or converge slowly
  ✗ Convergence can be much slower
  Example: Age (0-100) and Income (0-1,000,000)
           Income differences dominate similarity calculations

Algorithms that NEED Scaling:
  • Distance-based: K-NN, K-Means, SVM
  • Gradient descent-based: Linear/Logistic Regression, Neural Networks
  • Regularization-based: Ridge, Lasso (regularization unfairly penalizes large-scale features)

Algorithms that DON'T Need Scaling:
  • Tree-based: Decision Trees, Random Forest, XGBoost
  • Naive Bayes
  (These don't use distances and rely on splits/thresholds)

