1️⃣9️⃣  DATA LEAKAGE: Silent Performance Killer
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

What is Data Leakage?
  → Information from test/validation set "leaks" into training
  → Model performs great in development but fails in production
  → Most dangerous mistake in ML!

Common Causes:

1️⃣  SCALING BEFORE SPLIT
    ✗ WRONG: Scale all data → then split
    ✓ RIGHT: Split first → scale each set independently
    Why: Test statistics leak into training

2️⃣  FEATURE ENGINEERING ON FULL DATA
    ✗ WRONG: Create features from entire dataset → then split
    ✓ RIGHT: Split first → engineer features on training set only
    Why: Information from test set used for training

3️⃣  USING TEST DATA FOR HYPERPARAMETER TUNING
    ✗ WRONG: Tune using test set performance
    ✓ RIGHT: Use cross-validation or validation set
    Why: Model overfits to test set hyperparameters

4️⃣  INFORMATION FROM FUTURE
    ✗ WRONG: Use tomorrow's data to predict today (time series)
    ✓ RIGHT: Only use past/current data for predictions
    Why: Unrealistic scenario in production

