3️⃣4️⃣  REAL-WORLD SCENARIOS You'll Face
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

SCENARIO 1: UNBALANCED DATA
Problem: 95% negative, 5% positive cases
Your Solution:
  • Recognize problem (not just accuracy!)
  • Suggest: SMOTE, class weights, F1 metric
  • Show understanding of real-world impact

SCENARIO 2: LIMITED DATA
Problem: Only 1000 samples for classification
Your Solution:
  • Start simple (Logistic Regression)
  • Use cross-validation
  • Consider transfer learning
  • Understand overfitting risk

SCENARIO 3: PRODUCTION MODEL FAILS
Problem: Model works in notebook but fails in production
Your Solution:
  • Check data drift
  • Verify preprocessing consistency
  • Monitor inputs vs training data
  • Set up retraining pipeline

SCENARIO 4: STAKEHOLDER ASKS FOR ACCURACY
Problem: "Why only 85% accuracy? Make it 95%"
Your Solution:
  • Explain cost of false positives/negatives
  • Show appropriate metrics
  • Trade-offs: accuracy vs complexity
  • Business context matters

SCENARIO 5: MASSIVE DATASET
Problem: Data doesn't fit in RAM
Your Solution:
  • Use batch processing
  • Sample for EDA
  • Consider Spark/Dask
  • Streaming approaches

